xt":"கெண்மை","lemma":"கெண்மை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காணும்","parts":[{"text":"காணும்","lemma":"காணும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எனக்","parts":[{"text":"எனக்","lemma":"எனக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"காண்டகு","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"see"},{"text":"தகு","lemma":"taku","gloss":"worthy"}],"gloss":"worthy to be seen"},{"surface":"மொய்ம்ப","parts":[{"text":"மொய்ம்பு","lemma":"moympu","gloss":"strength"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"O"}],"gloss":"O strong one"},{"surface":"காட்டினை","parts":[{"text":"காட்டு","lemma":"kāṭṭu","gloss":"show"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"past"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ai","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you showed"},{"surface":"ஆகலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"āku","gloss":"become"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"verbal noun"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"because"}],"gloss":"therefore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"yāṉ","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"I indeed"},{"surface":"பிழைத்தனென்","parts":[{"text":"பிழை","lemma":"piḻai","gloss":"err"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"inflectional increment"},{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I erred"},{"surface":"சிறக்க","parts":[{"text":"சிற","lemma":"ciṟa","gloss":"flourish"},{"text":"க்க","lemma":"kka","gloss":"may"}],"gloss":"may flourish"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"ஆயுள்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயுள்","lemma":"āyuḷ","gloss":"life span"}],"gloss":"life span"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மிக்கு","parts":[{"text":"மிக்கு","lemma":"மிக்கு","gloss":"overflowing"}],"gloss":"overflowing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வரும்","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"varu","gloss":"come"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"which"}],"gloss":"which comes"},{"surface":"இன்னீர்","parts":[{"text":"இன்னீர்","lemma":"இன்னீர்","gloss":"sweet water"}],"gloss":"sweet water","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காவிரி","parts":[{"text":"காவிரி","lemma":"kāviri","gloss":"Kaveri river"}],"gloss":"Kaveri"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எக்கர்","parts":[{"text":"எக்கர்","lemma":"ekkar","gloss":"sand dunes"}],"gloss":"sand dunes"},{"surface":"இட்ட","parts":[{"text":"இட்ட","lemma":"இட்ட","gloss":"deposited"}],"gloss":"deposited","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மணலினும்","parts":[{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"maṇal","gloss":"sand"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even more than the sand"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed many"}]}],"literal":"To end the distress of those who live upon the earth, / bearing the heat of the sun with scorching rays, / with wind as food, whirling with the sun, / even the sages with shining matted hair are amazed, escaping the pounce aimed by the kite of curved wings / and sharp claws, entering inside him, the dove of short gait, / fearing death, entered the scale, / O descendant of the strong one of limitless generosity! / O younger brother of Kiḷḷi of generous chariots, who conquered foes with abundant strength of wealth, / O lord of warriors with curved bows and long arrows, O generous-handed lord of swift horses! I have a doubt. / All your ancestors who wore garlands of Bauhinia / did not do things that cause pain to Brahmins. And this, / 'Is it proper for you?' saying with displeasure, / even if you do not grieve at the offense I committed against you, / you felt ashamed indeed as if you erred! / To forgive those who wronged them is the lordly quality / of those born in this lineage, seeing their simplicity, / O strong one worthy to be seen, you showed it. Therefore, / I indeed erred. May your life span flourish / more than the sand deposited on the sand dunes / by the Kaveri of sweet water that comes overflowing!","translation":"O descendant of Sibi, the strong king of limitless generosity, who entered the scales to save a short-gaited dove that fled in fear of death from a sharp-clawed, curved-winged kite—an act of sacrifice that amazed even the sages of shining matted hair who live on wind and whirl with the sun, bearing its scorching heat to relieve the distress of earthly beings! O younger brother of Kiḷḷi, the lord of generous chariots who conquered foes with great strength! O lord of warriors with curved bows and long arrows, O generous patron of swift horses! I had a doubt. All your ancestors who wore Bauhinia garlands never did anything to hurt Brahmins. Yet, when I spoke to you with displeasure, asking, 'Is this proper of you?', you did not get angry at my offense; instead, you felt deeply ashamed as if you yourself had erred! You have shown the noble strength of your lineage, which easily forgives those who wrong them. Therefore, it is I who erred. May your life flourish for more years than the sands piled on the dunes by the sweet, overflowing waters of the Kaveri!","modern":"பூமியில் வாழ்பவர்களின் துன்பத்தைப் போக்க, சுட்டெரிக்கும் கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட சூரியனின் வெப்பத்தைத் தாங்கி, காற்றையே உணவாகக் கொண்டு, சூரியனுடன் சுழலும் ஒளிரும் சடைமுடி முனிவர்களும் வியக்கும்படி, வளைந்த சிறகுகளையும் கூர்மையான நகங்களையும் கொண்ட பருந்தின் பிடியிலிருந்து தப்பித்து, தன் மார்பில் அடைக்கலம் புகுந்த, மெல்ல நடக்கும் புறாவின் மரண பயத்தைப் போக்கத் தராசுத் தட்டில் ஏறிய எல்லையற்ற கொடையாளி சிபியின் வழித்தோன்றலே! பகைவர்களை வென்ற வலிமைமிக்க தேர்களை உடைய கிள்ளியின் தம்பியே! வளைந்த வில்லையும் நீண்ட அம்புகளையும் உடைய வீரர்களின் தலைவனே! வேகமான குதிரைகளை உடைய கொடைவள்ளலே! எனக்கு ஒரு சந்தேகம் இருந்தது. ஆத்தி மாலை அணிந்த உன்னுடைய முன்னோர்கள் அனைவரும் அந்தணர்கள் வருந்தும் படியான காரியங்களைச் செய்ததில்லை. ஆனால், நான் உன்னிடம் கோபத்துடன் 'இது உனக்குத் தகுமா?' என்று வெறுப்புடன் கூறியபோது, நான் செய்த பிழையை நீ பொருட்படுத்தாமல், நீயே தவறு செய்தது போல மிகவும் வெட்கப்பட்டாய்! தங்களுக்குத் தீங்கு செய்தவர்களையும் பொறுத்துக் கொள்ளும் பெருந்தன்மை இந்த வம்சத்தில் பிறந்தவர்களுக்கு மிக எளிதாக வரும் என்பதை உனது வலிமையால் காட்டினாய். அதனால், நானே தவறு செய்தேன். பெருகி வரும் இனிய நீரைக் கொண்ட காவிரி ஆறு குவித்து வைக்கும் மணல் துகள்களை விடப் பல ஆண்டுகள் உனது ஆயுள் சிறந்து விளங்குவதாக!","explanation":"This poem is addressed to Māvaḷattāṉ, the younger brother of the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi, by the poet Tāmappal Kaṇṇaṉār. The poet had previously spoken harshly to the prince during a game of dice, accusing him of acting unfairly, which was considered an offense. Instead of reacting with anger, the prince felt deeply ashamed, as if he himself had committed a mistake. Realizing his own error in misjudging the prince, the poet praises Māvaḷattāṉ's noble lineage, tracing it back to the legendary King Sibi (who sacrificed his own flesh to save a dove). The poet highlights how the quality of forgiving those who wrong them is inherent in this Chola lineage. He concludes by wishing the prince a long life, lasting more years than the sands deposited by the fertile Kaveri river.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}